    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** pacing the lineup at a stellar 81.88 efficiency score. His matchup against Burke is the ideal intersection of a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage (+14%), solidified by his prime #1 spot in the order. Joining him at the top of the production hierarchy, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.06) benefit significantly from the matchup against Baz; **Sam Antonacci** leverages a strong xwOBA of .374, while **Miguel Vargas** gains a subtle boost from Baz\u2019s slow delivery, which profiles as a green light for our secondary goal of securing stolen bases. **Heliot Ramos** (65.01) is also a strong play, as he faces a pitcher with a 4.68 xERA, the most favorable matchup among our starters, allowing his efficiency to climb despite a modest park factor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung**, whose 46.15 score placed him just outside our starting nine. While **Josh Jung** carries a respectable projection, his output is suppressed by a challenging matchup against Messick, forcing him to the pine in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Heliot Ramos** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, the latter of whom (60.36) remains a must-start despite facing a tough arm in Manaea due to his favorable dynamic platoon split. We are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (52.05) and **Brayan Rocchio** (50.86), both of whom are facing difficult left-handed starters; while the park conditions for **Jackson Merrill** are aided by wind, his heavy platoon disadvantage necessitates a watchful eye. Investors should keep a close watch on the weather and official lineups, as the current slate relies on **Andy Pages** and **Josh Lowe** to overcome negative park or skill-based adjustments to maintain our rotation's scoring floor.",
